Z||000003||Monkeyman||10-20-2000||05:38 AM||||John built it, had fun with it, and needs the cash to start another project.  He's currently in the middle of a truck project, but said that he would definitely be doing another Fiero.<P>18k <I>is</I> a lot of money, but this is one of the best cars out there.  Well worth the cash.  It is 99.999% perfect.  It has all of the right stuff, too.  John is a perfectionist with some incredible talent so I can guarantee that it's done right.  Besides, power cost money therefore 480 horses (at the crank) costs lots of money.||||reg||1
Z||000004||pollock||10-20-2000||09:42 AM||||I still have that '97 issue of high tech performance.  I remember being really blown away by that car.  It has changed a lot since.  It used to have this sweet comet-looking paint job and red and black leather interior with some (i guess PISA) custom dash.  <P>The dude who built it, if i recall, wasn't an engineer or even an experienced hot rodder... he worked in auto parts.  Just had the determination, and apparently the money, to do what people told him could not be done.  <P>Inspirational, yes... but if you read that whole ebay ad, he apparently got divorced last year.  One might only speculate as to why, hehe..........<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000005||Monkeyman||10-20-2000||08:27 PM||||Johns dash started out as a PISA unit, but he further customized it.  John Norman isn't an engineer although, since he built this car from the ground up all by himself, I guess you could call him an experienced hotrodder.  He owns NAPA auto parts in N. Manchester.  He's not rich, either.  (How many small business owners are?)  He created alot of the parts himself (especially for the N* conversion--no kits for him) and did all of the work which saved tons of money.  His divorce had nothing to do with his Fiero.  (I don't recall that being in the ad, but then I didn't read the entire ad.)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sleeper||10-21-2000||06:22 AM||||And it runs 11's on the 1/4 mile.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FIEROCIOUS||10-21-2000||04:25 PM||||Hey Monkeyman, Did you ever get those pics and talk to John for me? If not that's Ok I abandoned the idea, but it would be nice to post them for those who still have dreams!<P>And a note on John's Fiero; I did a TON of research on Northstar Fieros and all the contacts I made they all pointed to John as far a Northstar Fiero's go he is "THE MAN" ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||10-22-2000||07:47 AM||||Sorry, FIEROCIOUS.  I haven't had a chance to make the trip since I spoke to you last.  I've been way to busy at work.  Hopefully, I'll get a chance to make the trip before he sells the car.  <P>John <B>is</B> the man when it comes to N*s (or any customization).  He built Obsession from the ground up starting with a plain Jane coupe.  If he can't do it, it can't be done.  If I had the money (which I don't), I'd send the Grape Ape to him and have him customize it.  He manufactured his own N* adapter parts and designed the whole thing by himself.  About the only advantage he has over the average person is that he can get parts at cost since he owns an auto parts store.<P>I'll try to get up there in the next couple of weeks if my schedule allows it.||||reg||1
